WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.868
A cache holds 2 keys, and when it fills, the key used longest ago has to go.

00:07.868 --> 00:14.700
Keep the keys in a plain list and every call scans it to find one.

00:15.000 --> 00:18.784
Instead, pair two structures.

00:18.784 --> 00:31.700
A hash map jumps straight to a key’s node, and a linked list keeps the nodes from oldest to newest.

00:32.000 --> 00:38.133
Every get or put moves its node to the newest end.

00:38.133 --> 00:47.700
When the cache overflows, the node next to the head is the oldest, so it goes.

00:48.000 --> 00:50.555
Not one call scans.

00:50.555 --> 00:52.976
Each is O(1) time.

00:52.976 --> 00:59.700
That’s design: pick a structure for each question.
